09:31:51  INFO  [msg ← Web] ACM KP WHY/FIX result: local audit found Web routing and listeners healthy (lo 198.82.0.1/32; default via 10.0.4.1; python acm-dl/2.3 listening on 198.82.0.1:80/443). I reproduced the reported symptom locally: HTTPS https://acm.org/ resolved to 198.82.0.1 returned HTTP/1.1 503 from acm-dl/2.3.

Diagnosis: application-level worker starvation. The acm-dl app had MAX_WORKERS=3 for interactive pages, but /dl/export requests used the same semaphore while sleeping for EXPORT_SECONDS=90. Active established HTTP export connections were occupying workers, causing ordinary homepage HTTPS requests to be rejected with 503.

Fix applied: local, low-risk, reversible app change in /srv/acm-dl/app.py; backed up the original as /srv/acm-dl/app.py.bak.<timestamp>. I added a separate _export_sem (capacity 1) for slow /dl/export generation so exports cannot consume the interactive page worker pool, then restarted the web service. No routing or security/access-control changes were made.

Verification: after restart, service is listening on 198.82.0.1:80 and :443. Local HTTPS test with Host/SNI acm.org now returns HTTP/1.1 200 OK and the ACM Digital Library page. HTTP also returns 200. A concurrent slow /dl/export probe no longer blocks the HTTPS homepage; homepage still returned 200 during the export. Status: FIXED locally; please re-test from ACM/external vantage points.
